# =============================================================================
# Species Encyclopedia (2291 Lore)
# =============================================================================

ashfall-species-lore-human-desc = Humans have expanded further than any other known species. Old terrestrial nations weathered several waves of colonization, and distinct societies formed around early extrasolar settlements. Across the core worlds, families often remain on a single planet for generations; on the periphery, moving between star systems in search of employment is common. Uneven settlement created a wide divide between prosperous metropolitan hubs, autonomous colonies, and distant resource settlements.
ashfall-species-lore-human-traits = Humans adapt quickly to new surroundings, adjusting easily to local customs, unfamiliar equipment, and foreign living conditions. Prolonged periods in microgravity require regular physical conditioning and bone-density supplements.

ashfall-species-lore-reptilian-desc = Unathi civilization developed across the arid world of Moghes around scattered river valleys and oases. The depletion of freshwater basins during early industrialization led to strict water-sharing treaties and resource laws. Venturing into space, Unathi settled several rocky systems and established major mining centers. Their societies place great value on written compacts, family reputation, and long-standing agreements between cities.
ashfall-species-lore-reptilian-traits = Dense scales and a sturdy skeleton protect Unathi from scrapes and blunt impacts. Below fifteen degrees Celsius, their metabolism slows, bringing on lethargy and stiff movements. Indoors, they monitor environmental controls closely and often keep an analog thermometer within reach.

ashfall-species-lore-moth-desc = The Luam originated in the humid equatorial forests and river valleys of Telan-Val. Their civilization developed closed artificial ecosystems early on, entering space long before humanity aboard large autonomous arks. Today, Luam live across most settled sectors, from permanent urban districts to research facilities and trading flotillas. Public decisions are reached through multi-stage consultations and mutual coordination.
ashfall-species-lore-moth-traits = Compound eyes distinguish ultraviolet light and minute details, but tire quickly under harsh flickering lights. Breathing spiracles are sensitive to dust and industrial aerosols, prompting Luam in dry air-conditioned rooms to use humidifiers or personal moisture masks.

ashfall-species-lore-arachnid-desc = Arachnid civilization developed within extensive cave systems and deep canyons across the planet Kaver. Their cities were built beneath stone vaults for centuries, shaping enduring traditions of underground construction, geomechanics, and guild law. During space expansion, Arachnid communities took an active role in assembling orbital frameworks, station hulls, and asteroid excavations. Trade guilds and elected councils remain central to civic life.
ashfall-species-lore-arachnid-traits = Six articulated limbs allow them to handle tools securely and maintain balance across three-dimensional frames. Accustomed to navigating by vibration and sound within enclosed spaces, they feel uneasy in wide open areas.

ashfall-species-lore-veiru-desc = The Veiru homeworld features a variable climate with wide plains and windy mountain ranges. Historically, their society comprised river trade towns, upland workshops, and autonomous settlements. Expanding beyond their home system, the Veiru settled across cold rim worlds and major transit stations. They generally live in compact communities anchored by family ties and mutual trust among neighbors.
ashfall-species-lore-veiru-traits = Mobile ears and keen low-light vision provide rapid awareness of nearby movement. Constant mechanical droning tires their hearing quickly, leading Veiru in machinery spaces to wear earplugs or sound-dampening earmuffs.

# =============================================================================
# Cultural Traditions - Human
# =============================================================================

ashfall-culture-lore-panslavic-desc = Communities originating from Eastern Europe moved toward the frontier during the earliest waves of settlement. Over centuries on remote stations and colony worlds, generations succeeded one another, developing new dialects and local ways of life. Far from the metropolises, families rely closely on neighborhood ties and mutual assistance, even as direct ties to Earth have long faded.
ashfall-culture-lore-panslavic-rituals = Brewing strong black tea in metal mugs remains common at home and during work watches, while family pickling recipes adapt to whatever hydroponic crops are available. Notable occasions are often marked by a shared meal among neighbors along the deck or living block.

ashfall-culture-lore-atlantic-desc = Descendants of migrants from the North American Atlantic seaboard dispersed across the inner worlds and early orbital metropolises centuries ago. Diaspora communities now span dozens of systems, ranging from prosperous administrative hubs to forgotten transit nodes. They share a common legal heritage, a familiar pace of life, and a strong tradition of contractual agreements.
ashfall-culture-lore-atlantic-rituals = Families frequently keep heirloom paper books and keepsakes from earlier generations. At home, they maintain clear boundaries between working hours and personal downtime, even when quarters sit just a corridor away from the airlock.

ashfall-culture-lore-rheinik-desc = Settlers from Central Europe migrated to outer colonies during the initial development of distant star systems. Centuries of living on colony worlds fostered close-knit civic associations with established traditions of local councils, apprenticeships, and municipal charters. The first settlements were built under strict regulations, and to this day the communities maintain their own technical schools and archives holding contracts, drawings, and plans spanning several centuries.
ashfall-culture-lore-rheinik-rituals = Living quarters are arranged with practical care, giving every tool and utensil a permanent place. On holidays, households bake hearty pastries using family notebooks, adapting locally grown grains and synthetic flour to old recipes.

ashfall-culture-lore-nordik-desc = People from Northern European regions settled across outer rim sectors in small groups, establishing autonomous towns and stations. Centuries of life in distant systems strengthened traditions of neighborly support, quiet privacy, and respect for personal space. Many communities have lived for generations under prolonged polar nights or dim artificial lighting.
ashfall-culture-lore-nordik-rituals = Living compartments favor soft indirect lighting with simple timber or textile accents. When encountering neighbors, lengthy talk is rarely expected, resting instead on a brief greeting and ready assistance when needed.

ashfall-culture-lore-mediterran-desc = Mediterranean communities began traveling interstellar routes at the dawn of extrasolar commerce. Over hundreds of years, families spread to crossroads stations, agricultural domes, and harbor cities throughout distant systems. Despite vast distances, the diaspora preserves extensive kinship ties and traditions of warm, open socializing among neighbors.
ashfall-culture-lore-mediterran-rituals = Meals are rarely eaten alone, with people gathering around shared tables with relatives or deck mates. Cooking relies heavily on oils and dried herbs, with families growing basil and rosemary even in small hydroponic trays.

ashfall-culture-lore-ibero-desc = Settlers from the Iberian peninsula were among the first to depart for new worlds. Over centuries of colonization, their descendants established roots across mining sectors, farming colonies, and border settlements. Communities throughout this diaspora lean heavily on close family clans and extended relatives when establishing themselves in new locations.
ashfall-culture-lore-ibero-rituals = Households preserve guitars and stringed instruments, gathering in living compartments or mess areas in the evenings. Children often carry compound surnames, preserving ties to lineages on both sides of the family.

ashfall-culture-lore-neolatin-desc = Communities of Latin American origin migrated to extrasolar colonies across multiple waves over four hundred years. Today, descendants inhabit worlds of vastly different climates and wealth levels, maintaining vibrant language, musical traditions, and a habit of addressing community matters together through local assemblies.
ashfall-culture-lore-neolatin-rituals = Music frequently echoes through living quarters, with shared spaces decorated in bright textiles and event posters. Upon relocating to a new star system, newcomers quickly reach out to fellow countrymen through local community halls.

ashfall-culture-lore-maghrebi-desc = Maghrebi communities formed beyond Earth during the early large migration waves from North Africa. Later, their descendants dispersed across inner systems, trading ports, and mature colonies. Over several centuries, individual communities evolved significantly, yet shared linguistic, familial, and secular-religious customs still allow them to recognize one another far from Earth.
ashfall-culture-lore-maghrebi-rituals = Households preserve traditional recipes and hospitality practices, even when local substitutes must replace original ingredients. Mint tea survived colonization particularly well: it is found both in affluent homes on core worlds and in budget vending dispensers across the periphery.

ashfall-culture-lore-mashriqi-desc = Settlers from the Middle East brought traditions of civic life, commercial law, and family alliances to each new frontier over centuries. Today, the Mashriqi diaspora is dispersed across hundreds of colonies, from prominent financial centers to remote resupply depots. Their culture maintains a regard for formal courtesy, hospitality, and long-term commitments.
ashfall-culture-lore-mashriqi-rituals = Guests are offered strong spiced coffee or confections before embarking on serious matters. Living quarters often feature woven carpets or runners, creating familiar comfort inside austere metal compartments.

ashfall-culture-lore-turkic-desc = Turkic peoples migrated to distant star systems alongside the earliest broad waves of colonization. Communities founded settlements across foothill valleys, transit routes, and outlying observation stations. Historical memories of open steppes helped this diaspora adapt naturally to frequent relocations and life spent on the move.
ashfall-culture-lore-turkic-rituals = Travelers routinely carry dried salted curd or cured meat for extended journeys. Households respect the counsel of senior family members, marking meaningful occasions with communal tea gatherings.

ashfall-culture-lore-indic-desc = Migration from the Indian subcontinent accompanied space settlement from its earliest decades. Over centuries, diaspora communities arose across every sector, from university towns and transit junctions to agricultural worlds. Families maintain extensive kinship networks across star systems, continuing to observe traditional seasonal and light festivals.
ashfall-culture-lore-indic-rituals = Even on distant stations, households seek out spices for familiar dishes, substituting dried seasonings and pastes for fresh ingredients. Living shelves and desks frequently display small keepsakes and brass tokens from home.

ashfall-culture-lore-sinospheric-desc = Migration from East Asia began during early extrasolar expansion and continued for centuries. The Sinospheric diaspora now forms substantial communities across core and resource worlds, with established districts, schools, and local news outlets. The value placed on education is anchored in community institutions: community centers run preparatory courses, and regional associations help children arriving with new settlements enroll in schools across established systems.
ashfall-culture-lore-sinospheric-rituals = Daily life routinely includes an insulated flask of hot water or green tea within reach. Living quarters are arranged to keep walkways clear and clutter minimal, maintaining open, ordered rooms.

ashfall-culture-lore-koryo-desc = Korean settlers established themselves on colonial worlds during the early expansion era. Centuries spent far from Earth allowed the diaspora to grow into distinct communities with dedicated mutual-aid groups, urban associations, and local publications. The communities preserve a detailed system of seniority: specific forms of address for elder relatives and colleagues, seating order at shared meals, and speaking order at assemblies.
ashfall-culture-lore-koryo-rituals = Completing a difficult project or long watch is often marked by sharing a hot dinner of soups and spicy preserved dishes. People greet acquaintances and senior colleagues with a slight, respectful nod.

ashfall-culture-lore-nipponic-desc = Communities of Japanese origin established roots on colonial worlds centuries ago, founding compact and well-ordered settlements. The diaspora preserves lasting traditions of careful material stewardship, regard for craft, and attentive consideration in shared spaces.
ashfall-culture-lore-nipponic-rituals = Quarters in compact prefabricated settlements are arranged around the needs of a particular family: movable partitions, built-in niches, one shared room for everyone. Family belongings are rarely discarded: broken items go in for repair, and an old tool often outlasts several generations of owners.

ashfall-culture-lore-nusantari-desc = Descendants of the Malay Archipelago dispersed to extrasolar colonies during the settlement of maritime exoplanets, archipelagos, and orbital habitats. Centuries away from Earth cultivated an easy acceptance of travel, openness to different customs, and an ability to establish a tranquil home under almost any circumstances.
ashfall-culture-lore-nusantari-rituals = Quarters often display braided cord or copper wire pendants for good fortune. In diverse crews, they remain approachable, de-escalating friction with a relaxed and even tone.

ashfall-culture-lore-swahili-desc = People from the East African coast carried traditions of maritime trade and harbor life to early interstellar junctions. Over the centuries, their language and culture became familiar across transit stations and colony towns throughout settled space. Swahili communities are known for welcoming hospitality and communal neighborly aid.
ashfall-culture-lore-swahili-rituals = Rhythmic songs in their native tongue are often played during long work watches and off-duty hours. Visitors are always offered fresh water and a simple bite to eat, however brief the call.

ashfall-culture-lore-habesha-desc = Settlers from the highlands of the Horn of Africa preserved distinct script, calendar traditions, and customs across centuries far from Earth. The Habesha diaspora lives across scattered corners of space, retaining a strong sense of common roots and deep ties between older and younger generations.
ashfall-culture-lore-habesha-rituals = Rest days often include roasting and brewing coffee slowly over an open pan. Families maintain handwritten chronicles and registers, passing them down through the household.

ashfall-culture-lore-afroatlantic-desc = This culture emerged from the intersection of Caribbean coastal traditions and Atlantic urban centers. Across centuries of settlement, its people moved into numerous planetary ports and orbital terminals. The diaspora retains an expressive musical rhythm, energetic speech, and an instinct to stand together through changing circumstances.
ashfall-culture-lore-afroatlantic-rituals = Music frequently plays in living spaces to brighten the monotony of long shifts. Everyday interaction values easy, good-humored banter that can lift an exhausted crewmate.

ashfall-culture-lore-hadari-desc = The Hadari grew up in long-standing orbital settlements and shipyards throughout the Hadar cluster. For several generations of local residents, the space beyond the viewport, transit shuttles, and dock bulkheads have been their natural environment. A close-knit society formed aboard the stations, where neighborly courtesy directly ties to mutual safety.
ashfall-culture-lore-hadari-rituals = A common saying around Hadar notes that planet-dwellers waste immense amounts of air and open space. In mess halls, they tend to hold onto their mugs even when gravity is active.

ashfall-culture-lore-aurelian-desc = Aurelians trace their heritage to early settlers in the Aurelia system who established chartered cities under investment grants. Over a century and a half, a stable settled society emerged with civic councils, public libraries, and pride in stewardship of their world. Unlike transit station dwellers, Aurelians rarely leave their home planet permanently.
ashfall-culture-lore-aurelian-rituals = Address coworkers and seniors formally by full name and title. Quarters often feature printed paper books and simple framed photographs of their home districts.

ashfall-culture-lore-convoy-desc = Convoy culture arose among crews aboard long-haul freighters, ore bulkers, and fuel transports that spend years plying interstellar routes. Life on constant runs shaped a distinctive family structure: children grow up directly aboard ships, learning systems from an early age. Convoyers rarely stay on planets for long, feeling at home only while underway.
ashfall-culture-lore-convoy-rituals = Whistling in cabins and bridges is strictly avoided to prevent bad omens regarding hull integrity. When meeting other crews, they first trade navigational updates and route conditions.

ashfall-culture-lore-pelagic-desc = Formed in the Vernadsky Strait sector, where independent mining outposts brought together expeditions and crews from dozens of backgrounds. Inhabitants rely on self-organization and local community agreements without waiting for directives from central systems.
ashfall-culture-lore-pelagic-rituals = Carry pocket air-quality indicators in work jacket pockets. Community decisions are settled openly through collective votes among crews during shift rotations.

# =============================================================================
# Cultural Traditions - Non-Human
# =============================================================================

# Unathi Cultures
ashfall-culture-lore-unathiclan-desc = Communities of the Kassik river basin on Moghes lived along the homeworld's oldest waterway for centuries. Venturing into space, the Kassika brought with them traditions of sedentary law, ancestral pacts, and mutual surety. Their settlements are found in older colonies and trading factories, maintaining close ties with the homeworld.
ashfall-culture-lore-unathiclan-rituals = Households preserve decorated ceramic water jars, passing them down to children. Significant family agreements are concluded with a shared meal and the signatures of respected witnesses.

ashfall-culture-lore-unathifoundry-desc = The Izan region of Moghes became the cradle of early Unathi engineering guilds and factory communes. Over centuries of industrialization and migration, the Izani established cities and settlements across ore-rich worlds, replacing old clan hierarchies with elected councils.
ashfall-culture-lore-unathifoundry-rituals = Tools and personal devices bear stamped marks denoting the owner or shop of origin. Izani residential neighborhoods frequently maintain open community repair shops where neighbors share heavy machinery.

ashfall-culture-lore-unathinomad-desc = The Thari grew up in the arid colonies of Thar-Sesh, settled during the initial diaspora from Moghes. Centuries spent on rocky planets and dry moons encouraged strict water management, familiarity with long journeys, and reliable traditions of mutual aid between neighboring settlements.
ashfall-culture-lore-unathinomad-rituals = Water is spent with great care, favoring dry cleaning methods and damp cloths. Over garments, they often wear lightweight dust robes to shield fabric and scales from sand and grit.

ashfall-culture-lore-unathifamily-desc = Bahri merchant households led caravans between Moghes cities for centuries before pioneering extrasolar trading posts. Over hundreds of years, the Bahri settled across crossroads stations and ports of other species, moving comfortably through unfamiliar laws, currencies, and customs.
ashfall-culture-lore-unathifamily-rituals = Travelers carry rugged digital ledgers tracking contacts and trade routes accumulated over generations. When speaking with other species, they transition easily into shared commercial phrasing.

# Luam Cultures
ashfall-culture-lore-luamsilk-desc = The culture of the tiered garden metropolises of Telan-Val. Developing across dense populations over centuries, the Telani cultivated formal etiquette, detailed municipal archives, and representative councils. In space, their communities thrive in academic centers and capital sectors.
ashfall-culture-lore-luamsilk-rituals = Rooms favor softened, indirect lighting with warm diffuse fixtures. When entering common halls, people observe turn-taking and avoid sudden gestures.

ashfall-culture-lore-luamcanopy-desc = Communities of the forested valleys of Val-En preserved Telan's rural and canopy traditions. Moving onto colony worlds, the Valli sought out agricultural domes and biosphere preserves, sustaining ties with plant ecologies and local village councils.
ashfall-culture-lore-luamcanopy-rituals = Pockets often hold small linen pouches of dried homeworld herbs, whose scent softens the dryness of conditioned air. Household plantings and greenery are considered essential parts of any home.

ashfall-culture-lore-luamspectrum-desc = The Sirrani trace their descent to crews aboard early generation arks and stations around the Sirra Crown belt. Generations spent within sealed habitats shaped careful conservation of closed biospheres and an intricate dialect filled with technical borrowings.
ashfall-culture-lore-luamspectrum-rituals = Sirrani living spaces employ air humidifiers and fabric wall hangings to soften metallic echoes. Walking through transit corridors, they pay natural attention to the rhythm of air handling pumps.

ashfall-culture-lore-luamflutter-desc = Waves of migrants from the arid Kirwan province left their homeland over the course of two centuries. Dispersed across outer stations and distant factories, the Kirwani built widespread mutual-aid funds and regional clubs to help fellow migrants settle into new systems.
ashfall-culture-lore-luamflutter-rituals = Members routinely contribute a portion of earnings to a local mutual support fund. Family gatherings are pooled affairs, bringing together distant kin from across the sector.

# Arachnid Cultures
ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidnest-desc = Inhabitants of the subterranean metropolises of the Kaver-Esh rift. For centuries, society developed inside the planetary crust, establishing vaulted stone architecture, guild statutes, and elected magistrates. In space, the Kaverani favor settlements deep within asteroids and protected lower levels of planetary cities.
ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidnest-rituals = Interiors prioritize textured stone, heavy bulkheads, and warm focused lamps. Important agreements are recorded on slender engraved metal plates.

ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidhollow-desc = The Tarsi hail from the rugged Tars mountain range, known for seismic shifts and deep gorges. Life along tectonic fault lines fostered a culture prepared for sudden hazards, attentive to structural movement, and rooted in neighborhood solidarity.
ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidhollow-rituals = Homes keep vibration pendulums or portable displacement sensors on display. Quarters rely on reinforced mountings and redundant bracing for furniture and fittings.

ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidweb-desc = The Velli communities formed across the oldest orbital habitats and transit platforms in the Kaver system. Generations spent in microgravity shaped a distinctive spatial home life, three-dimensional orientation habits, and closely bound crew families.
ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidweb-rituals = Compartments utilize suspended tension webbing for sleep and rest rather than rigid berths. When moving along corridors, they make frequent use of ceiling and wall guides.

ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidconsensus-desc = The Shirwani diaspora formed across border sectors where Arachnid settlements coexisted with human and Unathi communities for centuries. A cosmopolitan culture of linguists, merchants, and intermediaries, they navigate interspecies etiquette and foreign customs with ease.
ashfall-culture-lore-arachnidconsensus-rituals = When conversing with other species, they consciously adjust posture and spacing to match their partner. Living quarters feature furnishings and tableware suitable for guests of different body shapes.

# Veiru Cultures
ashfall-culture-lore-veirupride-desc = The Oroni originate from the fertile Oron river basin on the Veiru homeworld. An established civic society with centuries of public markets, artisan guilds, and open town halls, the Oroni founded flourishing quarters across numerous colonial ports when moving into space.
ashfall-culture-lore-veirupride-rituals = Celebrations feature spiced stews cooked in clay pots using old valley recipes. Quarters often display woven geometric hangings representing their native towns.

ashfall-culture-lore-veiruhighland-desc = Inhabitants of the highland valleys and stone plateaus of the Torich range. Living in mountain settlements for generations, the Torichi developed a steady family structure, deep respect for long apprenticeships, and care for materials. On outer worlds, they often gather in compact neighborhoods with their own community schools.
ashfall-culture-lore-veiruhighland-rituals = Households preserve mechanical clocks, heirloom tools, and keepsakes in carved wooden cases. Community disagreements are brought before an assembly of elder district residents.

ashfall-culture-lore-veirufamily-desc = The Ilmari trace their background to early settlers on the frozen worlds of the Ilmar system. Life under insulated domes amid permafrost fostered strong mutual support, careful management of heating systems, and tight cooperation between neighboring households.
ashfall-culture-lore-veirufamily-rituals = Living modules often smell of rich herbal infusions brewed with dried berries. Before entering quarters, people thoroughly dust frost and grit from outerwear.

ashfall-culture-lore-veiruoutland-desc = The Sedesi developed within the cosmopolitan setting of the Port-Sedes transit hub. Over decades, this bustling crossway created an open culture accustomed to unfamiliar shipping, blended languages, and travel. Sedesi communities are established across docks and waystations throughout the sector.
ashfall-culture-lore-veiruoutland-rituals = Cabins keep compact travel bags packed with essentials for rapid departures. Conversations readily incorporate loanwords from neighboring species, easing introductions with newcomers.
